<title>SINGAPORE: World rice prices - October 31.</title>
<headline>World rice prices - October 31.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted by trading</p>
<p>and official sources in the key producing nations of Thailand,</p>
<p>Vietnam, India and the United States in U.S. dollars a tonne:</p>
<p>							     Oct 31    Oct 24</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 330-350  330-350 India-25 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB 240	240</p>
<p>India-15-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)  255-285   255-280</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port    275-285   275-280</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port     255-260   265-270</p>
<p>U.S.-California medium grain ($ per cwt) 19.50-20.50 19.50-20.50</p>
<p>U.S.-Long grain Arkansas ($ per cwt)     20.00-21.00 20.00-21.00</p>
<p>- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
</text>
